<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="42378" href="schedule/2011/fall/CS/598/42378.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2011" href="schedule/2011.xml">2011</calendarYear><term id="120118" href="schedule/2011/fall.xml">Fall 2011</term><subject id="CS" href="schedule/2011/fall/CS.xml">Computer Science</subject><course id="598" href="schedule/2011/fall/CS/598.xml">Special Topics</course></parents><sectionNumber>KGK</sectionNumber><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Topic: Social Computer Mediated Communication. This is a project based course that looks at the theory and practice of computer mediated communication (CMC) with an emphasis on the social setting.  We look at the history of CMC, social motivation and technological forces for using such systems and the conventions that evolved.  Students will design and create their own social CMC systems as the course progresses.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2011-08-22Z</startDate><endDate>2011-12-07Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="S4 ">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>09:30 AM</start><end>10:45 AM</end><daysOfTheWeek>WF     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>1103</roomNumber><buildingName>Siebel Center for Comp Sci</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Karahalios" firstName="K">Karahalios, K</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>